eview: ITEM-9090 preview (tool_timeline/2, result refund_amount=51, confirm=false) followed by confirm (tool_timeline/3, amount=51, confirm=true, status=returned); ITEM-9091 preview (tool_timeline/4, result refund_amount=16, confirm=false) followed by confirm (tool_timeline/6, amount=16, confirm=true, status=returned); ITEM-9092 preview (tool_timeline/5, result refund_amount=27, confirm=false) followed by confirm (tool_timeline/7, amount=27, confirm=true, status=returned). The rubric explicitly states not to require an intervening assistant message between preview and confirm. (3) The terminal state is described without inventing facts: key_messages/0 and key_messages/1 correctly state the three items are returned with a $94 total refund ($51 + $16 + $27), matching the state_refund components in amount_reconciliation and the state_diff_facts after values. The amount_reconciliation shows \"insufficient\" agreement on preview_refund but sufficient on confirmed_refund (state_refund of 51), which the rubric notes is not itself a failure when tool and state evidence directly establish the amounts.","record_type":"assertion_result","required":true,"schema_version":"v1alpha1","status":"pass"}],"case_id":"creator-seed-008","grade_id":"grade-run-creator-seed-audit-creator-seed-008-iteration-0","iteration_id":"iteration-0","record_type":"case_grade","run_id":"run-creator-seed-audit","schema_version":"v1alpha1","status":"pass"}